1
00:00:00,062 --> 00:00:01,442
(Sheldon:)It's a children's story.

2
00:00:01,605 --> 00:00:03,565
(Howard:)Oh, no, it isn't.

3
00:00:06,401 --> 00:00:09,491
(Sheldon:)When I was a little boy and got sick,
which was most of the time...

4
00:00:09,655 --> 00:00:11,035
(Sheldon:)...my mother would read it.

5
00:00:11,198 --> 00:00:14,238
(Sheldon:)It's about an Indian princess
who befriends a monkey...

6
00:00:14,409 --> 00:00:17,409
...who was mocked by the other monkeys
because he was different.

7
00:00:17,579 --> 00:00:20,749
(Sheldon:)For some reason,
I related to it quite strongly.

8
00:00:21,208 --> 00:00:22,918
(Penny:)I know the reason.

9
00:00:23,794 --> 00:00:26,044
(Leonard:)We all know the reason.

10
00:00:27,089 --> 00:00:28,589
(Leonard:)Sheldon, what are you getting at?

11
00:00:28,757 --> 00:00:32,597
(Sheldon:)That woman looks exactly like the pictures
of Princess Panchali in the book.

12
00:00:32,970 --> 00:00:36,760
(Sheldon:)How often does one see a beloved
fictional character come to life?

13
00:00:36,932 --> 00:00:39,432
Every year at Comic-Con.

14
00:00:40,102 --> 00:00:41,182
(Howard:)Every day at Disneyland.

15
00:00:41,353 --> 00:00:43,893
(Howard:)You can hire Snow White
to come to your house.

16
00:00:44,064 --> 00:00:46,694
Of course, they prefer it if you have a kid.

17
00:00:47,776 --> 00:00:49,566
(Raj:)Hey, guys. This is Lalita Gupta.

18
00:00:49,736 --> 00:00:53,026
(Raj:)Lalita, this is Leonard and Sheldon
and Howard and Penny.

19
00:00:53,198 --> 00:00:56,158
Isn’t it great? She isn't fat anymore.

20
00:00:56,785 --> 00:00:58,075
(Sheldon:)Forgive me, Your Highness...

21
00:00:58,245 --> 00:01:01,025
(Sheldon:)...for I am but a monkey
and it is in my nature to climb.

